(I wouldn't consider this to be a spoiler.)

There's no fixed plan, it rather depends on the actual game.
Generally; I explore each level in the main branch completely.
In the dark mines without light, I try to reach Minetown, where
I'll find light, and a lot of everything else.

Answer those questions for yourself while playing...
Do you need food, or is it likely that you shortly will need it?
Then enter the mines. Or if you are closer to Sokoban go there.
Are you still wimpy? Get ranged weapons, daggers from the gnomes
or darts from disarming the traps. A chance for good offensive
wands you'll find in Sokoban, and also defensive wands like fire
or lightning (sic!).
Is the first mine level dark and you have no light source? Then
do what you need from the up-stairs, or continue towards Sokoban.
Are you looking for armour? The mines provide your first kit.
Do you want some more rings and wands to have some more options
to survive the game? Do Sokoban.
Have you skipped (part of) the mines and still lacking something
essential? Complete the mines. (And get the luckstone.)
Are there monsters that you wouldn't survive blocking your way?
Retreat and try the other dungeon branch. Or, if you're still
missing something, dig past the critical level as a final resort.
Found the portal to Fort Ludios? If you have reflection (and
preferably also gloves and a fresh cockatrice corpse), clear the
area. If you don't have reflection, look for the amulet in Sokoban
or for the shield at Medusa's lair.
You need some dragon scales for better AC or other properties,
but you haven't found a special room with dragons? Consider doing
Ludios (but see preconditions above), or proceed to the Castle.

You see, that all very much depends on how a game evolves. Think
repeatedly about what you need in your game and where you'll most
likely get it.

